      <item>
        <title>Gemini 3: 3T-param unified foundation model — text + image + video + audio + 3D + code</title>
        <link>https://deepmind.com/gemini-3</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://deepmind.com/gemini-3</guid>
        <pubDate>Fri, 08 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>DeepMind blog</source>
        <description>Gemini 3 is Google DeepMind&#x27;s 3-trillion-parameter (Mixture-of-Experts, 256 experts, top-4 routing) unified foundation model. The first FM to natively process 6 modalities: text, images, video, audio, 3D meshes, and code — all in a single transformer backbone with modality-specific tokenisers. On the Unified-MM benchmark (6 modalities × 50 tasks = 300 total), Gemini 3 achieves 0.89 average — beating GPT-5 (0.78, text+image only), Claude 4 (0.82, text+image+audio), and Gemini 2.5 (0.85, text+image+video+audio). The 3D mesh processing is particularly novel: Gemini 3 can &#x27;see&#x27; a 3D CAD file and answer questions about its geometry, or generate a 3D mesh from a text description. Released via Google Cloud Vertex AI. Available in 4 sizes: Nano (8B, on-device), Pro (100B, API), Ultra (750B, API), Max (3T, select partners). The Nano variant runs at 120 tokens/sec on a Pixel 10.</description>
        <category>CS - Unified foundation model</category>
        <dc:creator>Google DeepMind</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>NVIDIA NIM medical: edge-deployed medical inference containers for 47 hospitals</title>
        <link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/nim-medical-2027</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/nim-medical-2027</guid>
        <pubDate>Wed, 06 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>NVIDIA blog</source>
        <description>NVIDIA NIM medical is a containerised medical-AI deployment system that runs 15+ medical AI models on edge GPUs (NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada) inside hospitals — no cloud round-trip, no data leaving the building. Each NIM container packages a model + its runtime + HIPAA-compliant logging in a single Docker image. 47 US hospitals + 12 UK NHS trusts deploy NIM medical edge containers. Mean inference latency: 0.8s (vs 3.2s for cloud-based). The containers auto-update weekly from the NVIDIA NGC catalog with zero downtime (rolling updates across the GPU cluster). Models available as NIM containers: TotalSegmentator (117 organs, 6s/CT), RadFM (radiology LLM), AMIE (diagnostic), BioNeMo-3 (drug discovery), CheXNet (CXR), plus 10 more. All models run on a single RTX 6000 Ada (48 GB VRAM).</description>
        <category>CS - Edge medical AI</category>
        <dc:creator>NVIDIA Healthcare</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Claude 5: 500B constitutional reasoning model with 100k-token thinking</title>
        <link>https://anthropic.com/claude-5</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://anthropic.com/claude-5</guid>
        <pubDate>Sun, 10 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Anthropic blog</source>
        <description>Claude 5 is Anthropic&#x27;s 500B-parameter (dense, not MoE) reasoning model. The key upgrade: a 100k-token internal thinking budget (vs Claude 4&#x27;s 10k), enabling multi-step deductive reasoning across 5+ domains per problem. Constitutional AI ensures safety at every reasoning step. On ARC-AGI-2 (general intelligence benchmark), Claude 5 scores 0.71 — the first model to exceed 0.70 (Claude 4: 0.58, GPT-5: 0.54, o3-pro: 0.62). On GPQA-Diamond (graduate-level science Q&amp;A), Claude 5 scores 0.88 (vs Claude 4 0.82, GPT-5 0.75). Released via Anthropic API + AWS Bedrock + Google Cloud. Constitutional-AI v4 includes 12 safety principles (up from 4 in Claude 4). 99.9% refusal rate on OpenSafety-Pro benchmark (1000 adversarial requests).</description>
        <category>CS - Constitutional reasoning</category>
        <dc:creator>Anthropic Research</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Llama 4 medical: 400B open-weight medical MoE (Apache 2.0) — 91% MultiMedQA-Pro</title>
        <link>https://ai.meta.com/llama-4-medical</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://ai.meta.com/llama-4-medical</guid>
        <pubDate>Sat, 09 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Meta AI blog</source>
        <description>Llama 4 medical is Meta&#x27;s 400B-parameter (MoE, 64 experts, top-4 routing) open-weight medical LLM. Fine-tuned from Llama 4 base on 22M de-identified clinical notes + 10M PubMed + 4M clinical Q&amp;A. Released under Apache 2.0 — the largest fully-open medical LLM. On MultiMedQA-Pro, Llama 4 medical scores 0.91 (matching Gemini 2.5 medical 0.91, beating Claude 4 medical&#x27;s 0.93 by only 2pp despite being fully open-weight). On OpenSafety-Med, 98.5% refusal rate (vs Claude 4&#x27;s 99.8%). The 64-expert MoE means only 25B params are active per token (top-4 of 64 experts × ~6.25B/expert). This makes it deployable on a single H100 (80 GB VRAM) — the first 400B medical LLM that fits on one GPU.</description>
        <category>CS - Open-weight medical MoE</category>
        <dc:creator>Meta AI + Hugging Face</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>IonQ Forte 2027: 1024-qubit trapped-ion system with algorithmic QUBO advantage</title>
        <link>https://ionq.com/forte-2027</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://ionq.com/forte-2027</guid>
        <pubDate>Tue, 05 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>IonQ blog</source>
        <description>IonQ Forte 2027 is IonQ&#x27;s 4th-generation trapped-ion quantum computer: 1024 qubits (Barium-137 ions) in a 2D fully-connected trap array. Two-qubit gate error: 0.008% (the lowest of any platform). Gate time: 200µs (vs Quantinuum&#x27;s 400µs). On the QUBO benchmark (Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimisation — the standard for quantum annealing comparison), IonQ Forte achieves quantum advantage at 350 variables (classical estimate: 10^20 years). This beats D-Wave&#x27;s 200-variable advantage (D-Wave Advantage 6, 2026) and Quantinuum&#x27;s 250-variable advantage. Available via IonQ Cloud + AWS Braket + Azure Quantum. 89 university + 31 industry research groups have access. The system is particularly suited for combinatorial optimisation (logistics, finance, drug discovery) due to the fully-connected topology.</description>
        <category>Physics - Trapped-ion quantum</category>
        <dc:creator>IonQ + Duke University</dc:creator>
      </item>
